      "writtenOn": "2022-05-13T07:04:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually you don\u0027t. If these were pointers to the struct then you would be correct, however as these are just plain structs then they are passed by value and copied everywhere. They are passed by value even when the struct is hidden behind an interface. So, every dependency that uses this tag gets its own copy.\n\nEquality is checked by comparing the value of each field in the struct.\n\nEven calls to methods like ExportMember pass a copy of the struct on the stack.\n\nWhile passing pointers would be more efficient I am not sure that the advantage is worth having in this case. If the struct was bigger and had more fields then it might.\n\nIf you want to change it to pass by pointer then you would need to:\n* Take the address of the struct when initializing these fields.\n* Change the type of the struct the methods are implemented on to *systemServerClasspathFragmentContentDependencyTag.",
